Prompt caching fundamentals
Model prompts often contain repetitive content, like system prompts and common instructions. OpenAI routes API requests to servers that recently processed the same prompt, making it faster and less expensive to reuse an exact prompt prefix than to process it from scratch. Prompt Caching works automatically for eligible requests, with no code changes required. It is enabled for all recent models,
gpt-4o
and newer.
This guide describes how prompt caching works in detail, so that you can optimize your prompts for lower latency and cost.
Caching best practices
Cache hits are only possible for exact prefix matches within a prompt. To realize caching benefits, place static content like instructions and examples at the beginning of your prompt, and put variable content, such as user-specific information, at the end. This also applies to images and tools, which must be identical between requests.
Keep instructions, tools, schemas, and shared context stable. Place request-specific content after the reusable prefix.
